### **Logical Relationships**
- **G1 -> G2, G3, G4 [AND]**  
  The main goal (deliver food and retrieve dishes) requires both delivery (G2/G3) and retrieval (G4) to be fulfilled.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [OR]**  
  Delivery via fetching (G3) can be achieved either by querying the inpatient's capability (G3.1) or coordinating assistance (G3.2).

- **G3.1 -> AT5 [AND]**  
  Querying retrieval capability (G3.1) requires executing task AT5.

- **G3.2 -> AT6 [AND]**  
  Coordinating assistance (G3.2) requires executing task AT6.

- **G4 -> G4.1, G4.2 [AND]**  
  Retrieving dishes (G4) requires opening the door (G4.1) and collecting dishes (G4.2).

- **G4.1 -> G4.1.1, G4.1.2 [OR]**  
  Opening the door (G4.1) can be done via human assistance (G4.1.1) or robot assistance (G4.1.2).

- **G4.1.1 -> AT8 [AND]**  
  Human-assisted door opening (G4.1.1) requires task AT8.

- **G4.1.2 -> AT9 [AND]**  
  Robot-assisted door opening (G4.1.2) requires task AT9.

- **G4.2 -> AT7 [AND]**  
  Retrieving dishes (G4.2) requires task AT7.

- **G2 -> AT1, AT2, AT3, AT4 [AND]**  
  Delivery via placement (G2) requires navigating to the room (AT1), placing food (AT2), tracking retrieval (AT3), and alerting on errors (AT4).

- **G5 -> AT3 [AND]**  
  Tracking meal retrieval (G5) is achieved by executing task AT3.
